{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018KtL3gUD1fFZMZm25JkESp","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## File Contents Report\n\n### 1. Software Requirements Document (srd004-ts.yaml)\n\n**Specific requirements requested:**\n\n**R4.3:** A custom format argument overrides the -s default format.\n\n**R5.1:** -m must use the system's monotonic clock (CLOCK_MONOTONIC via time.Now() in Go, which automatically uses the monotonic reading) instead of the wall clock for timestamp sampling.\n\n**R5.2:** -m is compatible with all format modes (-i, -s, default) and with custom format strings including subsecond extensions.\n\n**R5.3:** When -m is active, the timestamp must not jump backwards or exhibit discontinuities if the wall clock is adjusted (e.g., by NTP) while ts is running.\n\n**Non-goals section:**\n- cmd/ts does not implement egrep-style timestamp colorization.\n- cmd/ts does not read from files; it reads only from stdin.\n- cmd/ts does not support localized date parsing in -r mode (the Perl source explicitly notes this limitation).\n- cmd/ts does not implement --help or --version flags beyond a usage string on bad input.\n\n---\n\n### 2. cmd/ts/main.go\n\nComplete file contents (315 lines):\n\nThe file implements a timestamp command that:\n- Prepends timestamps to stdin lines with a default format of \"%b %d %H:%M:%S\"\n- Supports custom strftime format strings via a positional argument\n- Implements `-i` (incremental) mode showing elapsed time since previous line\n- Implements `-s` (since-start) mode showing elapsed time since startup\n- Handles subsecond extensions (%.S, %.s, %.T) for microsecond precision\n- Includes comprehensive strftime format specifier support (year, month, day, hour, minute, second, week numbers, weekday, composite specs like %T, %D, %F, %R, %r, %c, %x, %X)\n- Uses GMT timezone for elapsed time calculations\n- Installs a SIGPIPE handler to avoid crashes when stdout is closed\n\nKey implementation details:\n- Uses `time.Now()` for wall-clock timestamps\n- For incremental/since-start modes, creates a GMT zone and adds the delta duration to Unix epoch time\n- The `formatTime()` function manually implements strftime conversion without relying on Go's built-in time formatting\n- Supports padding modifiers (`-`, `_`, `0`) for numeric specifications\n\n---\n\n### 3. cmd/ts/ts_test.go\n\nComplete file contents (110 lines):\n\nThe test file includes:\n- Differential testing against the reference `ts` binary\n- A `TestDiff()` function running multiple test cases including:\n  - Default multiline, single line, partial last line, empty stdin\n  - Custom format variations (ISO, time-only, composite)\n  - Subsecond extensions (%.S, %.s, %.T)\n  - Incremental and since-start modes with various format options\n- Custom normalizers for subsecond and elapsed time patterns to handle variable timestamps\n- A `TestMutualExclusive()` function verifying that `-i` and `-s` flags are mutually exclusive\n- A `TestSIGPIPE()` function testing that the program handles SIGPIPE gracefully without blocking when stdout is closed\n\nThe tests use `testutils.BuildBinary()` to compile the Go binary and `testutils.RunDiffTests()` to compare output against the reference binary, applying normalization functions to ignore variable wall-clock timestamps."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bca9a522-19ae-4e2a-9d1e-372642e17e30","uuid":"0f53d908-b15e-4c6d-b600-de3793b69e10","timestamp":"2026-05-29T16:19:57.443Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to read three files to understand a task. Please read all of them fully and report their contents:\n\n1. `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5650/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd004-ts.yaml` - I specifically need the requirements R4.3, R5.1, R5.2, R5.3 and any non_goals section\n2. `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5650/cmd